Yeah you are, yeah you are. Switching to different articles was a big deal =
at the time more because we didn't politically know how to navigate changes=
 to the language, rather than something about the change in particular. Tha=
t particular change is extremely easy to ignore. Also there's other changes=
 between the literary dialect you'll find in books and the way Lojban's spo=
ken on the street that are far more substantial. But of course you'll get a=
 lot closer to being able to communicate with Lojbanists by reading those o=
ld texts, as we all learned by reading those same books or by hearing echoe=
s of them, and you'll find that we not only riff off that style a lot but e=
ven make lots of specific reference to those texts.

